          "Engage the Hispanic community with specificity on economic mobility and workplace protections: at 13.98% of the district and overrepresented in the renter population, Hispanic families are evaluating on whether Democratic representation is delivering real economic improvements, not on cultural acknowledgment. Workplace enforcement, housing access, and childcare affordability are the issues that drive turnout and candidate preference in this community.",
