          "Avoid positioning the opposition as ideologically alien or undeserving of engagement: the 47% in NE-LD-27 includes working-class and younger voters who are evaluating candidates on economic performance, not partisan identity. A challenger who can credibly argue that Republican governance would better serve younger renters and working families on housing, wages, or childcare has a clear path to 51%. Prokop's defense is economic performance and concrete delivery, not the assumption that demographic trends are automatically Democratic."
